-- BlogFlow CMS sample content (seed data)
-- Generated by scripts/make-seed.php — fictional demo content you can edit or delete.
--
-- What it adds: 3 categories (one nested), 10 tags, 2 author profiles, 8 posts
--   (6 published, 1 draft, 1 scheduled 7 days ahead), tags, related posts and media-free content.
-- What it does NOT touch: users/passwords, settings, theme, menus, existing posts.
--
-- HOW TO USE
--  1. Install BlogFlow first (the installer creates the tables).
--  2. If you chose a table prefix other than bf_, replace every `bf_ with `yourprefix_ , e.g.
--       sed 's/`bf_/`cms_/g' seed.sql > seed-cms.sql
--  3. Import: phpMyAdmin → select the database → Import → choose this file,
--       or: mysql -u USER -p DATABASE < seed.sql
--  4. In the admin: Settings → Backup & restore → Maintenance → Clear caches (or wait up to an hour).
--
-- Safe to run more than once: rows are matched by slug and existing rows are left unchanged.
-- Dates are relative to the moment you import. Featured images are not included — add them in
-- the editor (Media library uploads are files, not database rows).

SET NAMES utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
SET time_zone = '+00:00';

